  // Marco's bundled vendor spec-sheet table: what a model LINE supports (max RAM, slots, type, drive bays), as
  // opposed to what one unit's firmware reports. First matching entry wins, so specific entries (a form factor,
  // a generation) come before general ones. Matching: Manufacturer is the vendor key (see HardwareSpecTable.
  // VendorKey); Model is a wildcard pattern tested against the model string AND the product version (Lenovo's
  // friendly name); Chassis / Board are optional patterns; ModuleFormFactor requires the host's installed modules
  // to report that form factor (how Dell Micro units are told apart from Tower/SFF when the model string is the
  // same for all three). Entries with no facts deliberately exclude a sub-model from a broader pattern.
  // Bay counts are the spec sheet's "up to" figures — many chassis trade one bay type for another.
  // "verified" in Source = read from the vendor manual for this table; otherwise transcribed from spec sheets.
